    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "This project was concerned with the development of approaches that can be utilized to\r\ndetermine the drift and ductility demands and capacities for high-rise buildings and to\r\nimprove seismic design practice through the explicit incorporation of ductility and drift\r\ncontrol in the preliminary design process. To achieve this objective, emphasis was placed\r\non (a) a review and evaluation of the state-of-the-practice in ductility and drift based\r\nearthquake resistant design, (b) an evaluation of the damage potential of recorded ground\r\nmotions, (c) in-depth studies of the seismic performance of three high-rise reinforced\r\nconcrete frame buildings, including accurate analytical modeling, nonlinear time-history\r\nanalysis, assessment of predicted and recorded responses, and evaluation of detailing, (d) a\r\nstudy of member detailing requirements, and (e) the development of a conceptual design\r\napproach.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Tanaka, Nobumasa and Inoue, Norio and Fukuda, Takaharu and Hatamoto, Hitoshi and Sunasaka, Yoshio and Ohrui, Satoshi and Tsujimoto, Tetsuya and Bertero, Vitelmo V and Hart, Gary C and Anderson, James C and Krawinkler, Helmut and Moehle, Jack P and Miranda, Eduardo and Nassar, Aladdin and Rahnama, Mohsen and Ekwueme, Chukwuma G and Sabol, Thomas A and Qi, Xiaoxuan. (1992). Design Guidelines for Ductility and Drift Limits. CUREE-Kajima Research Project Reports CKI-08, CKI-09, CKI-10, and CKI-11. Stanford Digital Repository. Available at: http://purl.stanford.edu/mf043hm5659",
            "type": "preferred citation",
            "identifier": [],
            "displayLabel": "Preferred Citation",
